From 4924464e1654dea23882314b073a253ccccc0a3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: riotashley81-jpg <riotashley81@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:17:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Render passes: pass worker helper process and late passes

A title can run a pass's guest work in a second copy of the executable
(--pass-worker, headless) on another core. The main process submits the
kept machine state and a job; the helper loads it as a savestate load
would, runs the job with guest time frozen and returns the RAM pages,
scratchpad and PGXP shadows it changed. psx_mod_render_pass_open opens a
frame's generation without a pass, and psx_mod_render_pass_late adds an
image to it once the result is in, even after the flip. Motion sets can
export their blended values for the helper (psx_motion_export).

Generations are now dumped (render_pass_dump) when they leave the screen,
so late images are included. TCP pass_worker_stats.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
