+## Running the replay in a helper process (pass worker)
+
+A pass that replays the draw section costs about as much host time as the
+game's own draw, on the same thread. A title can move that guest work to a
+second copy of the executable running headless on another core
+(`pass_worker.c`, Windows; `mod_plugins.h` `psx_mod_pass_worker_*`):
+
+- The plugin registers its job function in its constructor
+  (`psx_mod_pass_worker_set_job`); it runs in both processes, and only the
+  helper calls it. `psx_mod_pass_worker_start` launches the helper
+  (`--pass-worker NAME PID --headless`, no debug port, no heartbeat, its
+  console output in `%TEMP%\psxrecomp_pass_worker\helper_log.txt`).
+- At the pass point the plugin plans as usual, opens the frame's generation
+  without running a pass (`psx_mod_render_pass_open`), and submits the kept
+  machine state (main RAM, scratchpad, CPU and GTE registers) with an opaque
+  job: for a blended replay, the values `psx_motion_export` gives, which the
+  helper writes back with `psx_motion_write_value` where the in-process pass
+  would have applied them.
+- The helper loads the state as a savestate load would (RAM, the dirty-code
+  bitmap, then `overlay_watch_invalidate_after_ram_restore`), runs the job
+  with guest time frozen, and returns the 4 KiB RAM pages that changed, the
+  scratchpad and the PGXP shadows the job wrote (`pgxp_pass_export`). Between
+  jobs it lets one frame of device time pass so a transfer a job started
+  never stays busy.
+- Later, once the display shows that frame, the plugin calls
+  `psx_mod_render_pass_late`: its callback restores the kept state, puts the
+  helper's result on top (`psx_mod_pass_worker_apply`, which imports the PGXP
+  shadows through the pass journal) and submits the OT. The image joins the
+  generation on screen, or the pending one if the flip has not been seen yet;
+  an image that misses its phase's deadline is not shown.
+
+`pass_worker_stats` (TCP) reports jobs submitted / done / late / failed, the
+last job's helper time, pages and PGXP slots. A helper that exits (a runaway
+job hits its watchdog) ends the worker for the session; the title falls back
+to in-process passes.
+
